'' TKO0999 for std/chrono's ToLocaleDateString / ToLocaleTimeString / ToLocaleString called
'' through the TYPE, as reported: each lowered with no receiver and segfaulted, lsShort as much
'' as lsLong. The same calls on an object, and the static WeekdayName, are accepted. See
'' symbols/staticcall.tiko and diagnostics/nonstatic-type-call.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -c tests/diagnostics/src/chrono-static-call.tiko
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 1
'' EXPECT-OUT: chrono-static-call.tiko(7,22): error TKO0999: 'tolocaledatestring'
'' EXPECT-OUT: chrono-static-call.tiko(8,22): error TKO0999: 'tolocaletimestring'
'' EXPECT-OUT: chrono-static-call.tiko(9,22): error TKO0999: 'tolocalestring'
'' EXPECT-OUT: chrono-static-call.tiko(10,22): error TKO0999: 'tolocaledatestring'
'' EXPECT-OUT: chrono-static-call.tiko(11,22): error TKO0999: 'tolocaletimestring'
'' EXPECT-OUT: chrono-static-call.tiko(12,22): error TKO0999: 'tolocalestring'
'' EXPECT-NOT: chrono-static-call.tiko(14,
'' EXPECT-NOT: chrono-static-call.tiko(15,
'' EXPECT-NOT: chrono-static-call.tiko(16,
'' EXPECT-NOT: chrono-static-call.tiko(17,
'' EXPECT-NOT: chrono-static-call.tiko(18,
'' EXPECT-NOT: chrono-static-call.tiko(19,
'' EXPECT-NOT: chrono-static-call.tiko(20,
'' EXPECT-MAX-DIAG: 6
